{"id":"082ae2cac9195779a8a62e5d8a393bf5a4b63aa4","axis":"silent","repo":"phan/phan","sha":"082ae2cac9195779a8a62e5d8a393bf5a4b63aa4","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"NEWS.md","lines":["@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@ New features:"," "," Performance improvements:"," - Reduce analysis overhead without changing the emitted issues: FQSEN and `Type` memoization no longer allocate a closure per lookup, `FullyQualifiedClassName::fromType()` is cached per type, `UnionType` string conversion and equality checks are faster for small type sets, whether a file is excluded from analysis is cached per path (and issues in excluded files are no longer formatted before being discarded), the `clone` AST normalization pass is skipped for files that do not contain `clone`, and redundant `realpath()`/stat calls were removed.","+- Reduce the cost of inherited methods in the class and method analysis phases (large on projects with many inherited methods) without changing the emitted issues: resolving `static` in a union type returns immediately when none of its types can change (no `Context` is created), finding the methods that a method overrides does one lookup per ancestor class instead of three and no longer creates a method FQSEN per ancestor, an ancestor's template parameter type map is fetched once per ancestor instead of once per inherited method, and creating method/property/class constant FQSENs no longer builds a string cache key (or lowercases method names that cannot be magic methods)."," "," Bug fixes:"," - Analysis workers of `--processes N` now terminate without running PHP's shutdown sequence once they have sent their results to the parent (by exec'ing `/bin/true`). Destroying the inherited heap wrote to every object, which copied the copy-on-write pages shared with the parent and the other workers (several GB per worker on large projects) and delayed the parent's output by seconds. Set `PHAN_DISABLE_FAST_EXIT=1` to keep the regular `exit()`; it is also kept when the profiler, xdebug or pcov is active. Analysis results are unchanged."],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Phan/CodeBase.php","lines":["@@ -1259,6 +1259,23 @@ public function getMethodByFQSEN(","         );","     }"," ","+    /**","+     * Equivalent to hasMethodWithFQSEN() followed by getMethodByFQSEN()","+     * for the method named $lowercase_name (with alternate id 0) in the class $fqsen,","+     * without creating the method FQSEN.","+     *","+     * @param string $lowercase_name the lowercase name of the method","+     * @return ?Method the method, or null if the class has no method with that name.","+     */","+    public function getMethodByClassAndLowercaseName(","+        FullyQualifiedClassName $fqsen,","+        string $lowercase_name","+    ): ?Method {","+        return $this->getClassMapByFullyQualifiedClassName(","+            $fqsen","+        )->getMethodByLowercaseName($lowercase_name);","+    }","+","     /**","      * @return array<string,Method>","      * The set of methods associated with the given class"],"additions":17,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Phan/CodeBase/ClassMap.php","lines":["@@ -126,6 +126,14 @@ public function getMethodByName(string $name): Method","         return $this->method_map[\\strtolower($name)];","     }"," ","+    /**","+     * Fetches the method with the lowercase name $lowercase_name (including any alternate id suffix), if it exists.","+     */","+    public function getMethodByLowercaseName(string $lowercase_name): ?Method","+    {","+        return $this->method_map[$lowercase_name] ?? null;","+    }","+","     /**","      * @return array<string,Method>","      */"],"additions":8,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Phan/Language/Element/Clazz.php","lines":["@@ -1976,11 +1976,17 @@ public function getConstantMap(CodeBase $code_base): array","      * @param Option<Type> $type_option","      * A possibly defined type used to define template","      * parameter types when importing the method"